id:                     E431
trigger_tool: conan|git-apply|patch-ng
phase: patch-replay|source-verification
error_signature: reverse patch fails because Conan source cache was mistaken for patched postimage
severity: 2
category:               conan, source-boundary
match_keywords: Conan source folder, pristine source, patch postimage, reverse replay, /dev/null addition, ordered patches
title: Prove whether a Conan source cache is pristine before patch replay
root_cause: A successful Conan build can apply patches in a separate build copy while retaining pristine downloaded bytes in the cache source directory. The directory name and build log do not establish postimage semantics.
affected_scope: Offline or local patch replay that reuses a Conan cache source tree instead of re-extracting the official source archive.
verification_cmd: Inspect one modified upstream target and one patch-added target, then copy existing pristine targets, require every missing target to be a declared /dev/null addition, apply patches once in order, and verify final inventory and hashes.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: byte-proven-pristine-forward-replay
rec_description: Determine cache semantics from exact bytes. If pristine, copy only existing preimages, leave declared additions absent, and apply the current ordered patch set exactly once.
rec_command: compare known preimage/postimage anchors; forward-apply all patches; verify target count and postimage hashes
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: official-archive-create-new-replay
fallback_description: When cache semantics cannot be proven, extract the hash-verified official source into a new isolated root and replay there.
fallback_command: verify source archive SHA256, extract create-new, apply ordered patches
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: reverse.*patch.*conan.*source|assume.*source.*postimage
forbid_1_reason: Reversing patches against pristine sources fails or corrupts the replay premise.
forbid_1_consequence: A partial tree can be mislabeled as a verified upstream reconstruction.
forbid_2_pattern: precreate.*missing.*target.*without.*dev/null
forbid_2_reason: Missing cache paths are valid only when the exact patch set declares them as additions.
forbid_2_consequence: Typos or omitted upstream inputs are hidden by synthetic empty files.
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: []
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
